course: dictionary
lesson: 1278
title: Small word, big job: but
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «But» is a tiny word with a big job. Most of the time it joins two ideas that are different or surprising. «Sound travels through air, water and solids, but not through empty space.» The first half tells you where sound goes, and the second half tells you where it does not. «But» shows the turn between them.
explain: «But» can also mean except. «He ate all but one biscuit.» He ate every biscuit apart from one. Check by swapping in except: «He ate all except one biscuit» still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: In a story, «but» often shows a problem or a protest. «But Mum, I only had two!» The child is pushing back. Notice the feeling behind the word, not just its place in the sentence. In formal writing, you may see «however» or «whereas» doing the same job.
fact: «But» joins two ideas that contrast, or that surprise us when they come together.
fact: «But» can mean except, as in «all but one».
fact: «Buts» (a noun) means objections or reasons why not, as in «no ifs or buts».
fact: In Scotland, Ireland, Australia and New Zealand, «but» at the end of a sentence can mean «though»: «It's cold, nice day but.»
fact: Exam words that do the same job as «but» are «however», «nevertheless», «whereas» and «with the exception of».
exercise: «Sound travels through air, but not through empty space.» What does but show? | Two things that are the same | *A contrast: one thing is true and the other is not | A question about sound
exercise: «He ate all but one biscuit.» What does but mean here? | Loudly | *Except | Also | Quickly
exercise: Jayden says, «No buts, just tidy your room.» What does buts mean? | *Objections or reasons why not | Extra cakes | Feet | Bruises
test: «Leaving a group can feel scary, but trusted adults can help.» Which word could replace but and keep the meaning? | Because | Like | Before | *However
test: «Dodging a question isn't the same as lying, but it can hide things.» What does but do in this sentence? | It means except | It adds a list of things | *It shows a contrast: dodging is not lying, yet it can still hide things | It asks a question
exam: «Her brother is quiet, but she is loud.» Which exam word could replace but? | *Whereas | Also | Because | Under
